# Machine-local working files: provider binaries, state, crash dumps. State is
# whatever the backend resolves to — the S3 block in versions.tf, or a local
# backend if an (also ignored) backend_override.tf is present. Either way the
# state itself never belongs in git.
#
# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored — it's a dependency
# manifest, not scratch (the go.sum of this directory). Tracking it pins the
# exact provider build the stack was last validated against, rather than
# letting every clone re-resolve the `~> 6.56` range to a different 6.x. It
# also makes constraint/lock drift show up as a PR diff: dependabot bumps the
# constraint in versions.tf but does not maintain the lock, and the two silently
# disagreed for five days in Jul 2026 until a `tofu init` failed on it.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Plan output
*.tfplan

# Variable overrides with secrets
*.auto.tfvars
*.tfvars
backend_override.tf

# tofu plan artifact from `make infra-plan`
tf.plan

# Written by cloud-dev-up: the image tag cloud ran BEFORE the test apply, so
# cloud-dev-down can restore it exactly. Local state about a local experiment.
.cloud-dev-prev-tag
